\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Lord, enlarge our scanty thought
\par To know the wonders Thou hast wrought;
\par Unloose our stammering tongues, to tell
\par Thy love immense, unsearchable.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. What are our works but sin and death,
\par Till Thou Thy quickening Spirit death,
\par Thou giv'st the power Thy grace to move:
\par O wondrous grace! O boundless love!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How can it be, Thou heavenly King,
\par That Thou shouldst us to glory bring;
\par Make slaves the partners of Thy throne,
\par Decked with a never-fading crown?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Hence, our hearts melt, our eyes o'erflow,
\par Our words are lost; nor will we know,
\par Nor will we think of aught beside,
\par My Lord, my Love is crucified!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. First-born of many brethren Thou;
\par To Thee, lo! all our souls we bow;
\par To Thee our hearts and hands we give:
\par Thine may we die, Thine may we live!
\par                                              Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

